      "writtenOn": "2025-06-11T15:45:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Meta suggestion:\nIt would be valuable to have a comment outlining the process for:\n* Updating the core Vulkan version (i.e., check for existing features/extensions currently utilized that got promoted and update logic accordingly)\n* Adding support for a new Vulkan feature / extension \n    * explaining the meta structure of the relationship between `DeviceExtensions` and how that relates to `FeaturesToAdd` - you have some of this below where you mention device extension support for determining features we can or cannot add, but having one large comment doc at the top of this file seems like a good idea.\n    * The process of incorporating it: adding it to the preferred features test, adding the extension bool to `DeviceExtensions`, adding a feature enabling bool to `FeaturesToAdd`, where else one would need to add additional checks into these helpers\n\n\nPerhaps add an `SkASSERT` that the vulkan version is not \u003e1.4 somewhere in here such that if the version *does* get upgraded, the assert will fail, signaling to the person updating it that processes should be followed + things updated here? (Same within the test file for this)",
